# Folio

A small, account-free reading library built with Next.js.

## Run locally

"'```sh
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open http://localhost:3000. The starter shelf contains labeled sample books; open any book and choose **Remove book** to clear it. Add your own books, mark them finished, and keep notes on each book'"'s page. Each book has a direct URL and a share button.

Books are stored in "'`data/books.json`. Changes survive application restarts as long as this file remains on persistent, writable storage. Set the `BOOKS_FILE` environment variable to use a different file path. For production, run `npm run build` and `npm start` on a Node.js server with persistent storage; ephemeral or read-only serverless filesystems are not suitable. A shared link is reachable by someone else only when the app is hosted at a URL they can access. Anyone with access to the app can view and change the library because there are no accounts.
EOF
